course: dictionary
lesson: 10861
title: Vicar and church words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vicar is a priest in charge of a church and the local area around it, called the parish. You may meet this word in stories about village life. When you do not know a word, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues.
explain: «The vicar says God knows each heart better than we do.» The word says tells you the vicar is a person who speaks and teaches, so a vicar is someone who explains church ideas to people. Check by putting your meaning in the sentence: "The priest says God knows each heart better than we do." It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: In British comedy and stories, «the vicar» can also be a joke character: a polite, kind, slightly old-fashioned church person at tea parties and village fêtes. The clues are the setting. A tea party or a fête tells you the story is light and friendly, not serious. Context helps you choose the right meaning.
fact: A vicar is a priest in charge of a church and its parish.
fact: A vicarage is the vicar's house.
fact: In British village life, a vicar leads services, weddings and funerals, and helps at the church fair.
fact: Priest, minister, pastor, rector and curate are related words for church leaders.
fact: In stories and comedy, «the vicar» can be a polite, kind, slightly old-fashioned person, often at tea parties and village fêtes.
exercise: What is a vicar? | A kind of bird | A river that runs through a village | A shop that sells tea and cakes | *A priest in charge of a church and its local area
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the vicar's house. | vicar | church | parish | *vicarage
exercise: «The vicar says God knows each heart better than we do.» What does the word says tell you about the vicar? | The vicar is asleep in the church | The vicar is a shopkeeper | *The vicar is speaking and explaining ideas to people | The vicar is singing a song
test: In British village life, what does a vicar lead? | Bus timetables | Fishing trips | Football matches | *Services, weddings and funerals
test: In a joking British story, «the vicar» is best described as? | *A polite, kind, slightly old-fashioned church person | A rude stranger | A robot that makes tea | A pirate captain
exam: Which word is NOT a related word for a church leader? | *Garden | Priest | Minister | Pastor
